# Testing Strategy

This rule defines testing STANDARDS. For the agent's behavioral contract when writing tests, see `agents/tester.mdc`.

## Stack

| Layer | Tool | Focus |
|-------|------|-------|
| **Unit** | Vitest | Pure logic, edge cases, validators |
| **Integration** | Vitest + MSW/supertest | API flows, state transitions |
| **No e2e** | — | Too slow, too brittle for our stage |

## Distribution Target

- 70% failure/edge case paths
- 30% happy path / smoke

## Naming Convention

`it('returns 400 when email is missing')` — tests as sentences, not labels.

## Hard Rules

1. Every bug fix starts with a failing test (red → green).
2. Mock boundaries only (APIs, DB, filesystem). Never mock your own modules.
3. Test behavior, not implementation. Test "what happens" not "which function was called."
4. One logical assertion per test.

## What NOT to Test

- UI layout/styling (visual regression is V2)
- Third-party library internals
- Simple getters/setters with no logic
- Configuration files
